      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this implementation is going to need a couple of options. I don\u0027t think we\u0027re going to be able to get away with a single configuration option without making some assumptions like we do with Fernet.\n\nWe can do a couple of things.\n\n1.) We have a single directory which contains only keys for validating tokens. We also have a signing key in a known, hardcoded, location. For example, the directory could be /etc/keystone/jwt-keys/validation-keys/ and the signing key could be /etc/keystone/jwt-keys/private.pem.\n\n2.) We have a single directory for validation keys and a configuration option pointing keystone to the signing key.\n\nThe first option isn\u0027t as complicated and doesn\u0027t require deployers to understand more options than required. Certificate rotation requires a renaming strategy that goes hand-in-hand with distribution across nodes.\n\nThoughts?",
      "range": {
